Package: @alchemy.run/domain
Applies-to: vendor/alchemy/alchemy.run-domain-734c27a.tgz
Upstream: not yet reported
Why: A text's length written into a template (`${cmd.text.length}:${cmd.text}`) ends the whole proof with "z3 cannot
  read back (str.len …): nothing declares it", naming no file and no line. With this the code is read: a rule that
  holds is proved, and a broken one comes back with the text that breaks it.
Remove-when: The library reads back an argument that is itself computed. `bun run beep patches prove` then says this
  patch's test passes without it.
Test: test/alchemy-domain/02-text-length-in-a-template/TextLength.test.ts

